  "visibility": "unlisted",
  "description": "Verified ESP32-C3 + 2x PCA9685, IMU and ToF firmware twin; companion 20-DOF MuJoCo physics and 27-part KernelCAD geometry. NOT yet a coupled firmware-to-physics simulation.",
  "readme": "# AXIOM H1\n\n20-channel robot controller on ESP32-C3, 2\u00d7PCA9685 at 0x40/0x41, VL53L0X at 0x29, MPU6050 at 0x68, and emergency-stop input.\n\n**Actual physics reference:** 20-actuator free-base MuJoCo 3.3.7 model with gravity and collision, tested against standing, arm wave, obstruction stop and motor shutdown, source on work-1 under `/data/axiom-h1/labwired/examples/axiom-h1/`.\n\n**KernelCAD geometry:** https://app.kernelcad.com/p/QC9kIRT9?version=1\n\n**Live LabWired firmware lab:** https://app.labwired.com/?share=PUDy_Tg6Yvzo&run=1\n\n**Limitations:** LabWired firmware simulation is not yet physically coupled to MuJoCo. No verified walking, torque hardware parity, brown-out, independent servo power distribution or factory readiness. Motor-disabling emergency stop permits the free-base robot to fall; actual hardware requires safe support/braking."
}
